  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Details are small sounds on top of the bed: the buzz of a tube, a drip, a vending machine. They make a place specific. Pitch changes the speed of playback: at 2 the clip plays twice as fast and an octave higher, at 0.5 half as fast and an octave lower.\r\n\r\n<b>Predict:</b> The drip loop plays at Pitch 1, with one drop every 4 seconds. At Pitch 0.5, how do the drips change, in sound and in rhythm?\r\n\r\n<b>Try:</b>\r\n1. Set the Pitch of \"Detail \xB7 Drip\" to 0.5, then to 1.5.\r\n2. Duplicate \"Detail \xB7 Drip\" and set the copy's Pitch to 0.8: now there are two drips.\r\n3. Tick the Audio Source of \"Detail \xB7 Vending Machine\" and set its Volume so that it sits under the hum.\r\n\r\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Asset Library, Sounds/Soundscape/Details</color></size>"
