      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The scene is heard through the Audio Listener, a component on the camera. A scene has only one. Every Audio Source plays its clip into it. Here every source is 2D (Spatial Blend 0): it sounds the same wherever the camera is. Each source is placed only so you can find it.



    <b>Predict:</b> Every source here is 2D. If you move the Listener camera to the far end of the underpass, what changes in what you hear?



    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Enter Play mode and listen from Camera - Listener.

    2. Move Camera - Listener to the far end, at z 46, and listen again.

    3. Disable its Audio Listener component, then enable it again.



    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Unity Manual: Audio Listener, Audio Source</color></size>'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
