  m_text: "Several Audio Sources playing at once are layers, mixed by the engine. Each source's Volume, from 0 to 1, sets its share of the whole. A soundscape usually has a quiet bed, a mid layer such as a hum, and a few details on top. No Audio Mixer is needed for this.\r\n\r\n<b>Predict:</b> The ventilation hum plays at Volume 0.3. If you set it to 1, which of the other layers can you still hear clearly?\r\n\r\n<b>Try:</b>\r\n1. Set \"Mid \xB7 Ventilation Hum\" to Volume 1, then to 0.\r\n2. Tick Mute on one source at a time to hear what each one adds.\r\n3. Balance the layers again: the beds around 0.3\u20130.5, the hum 0.3, the details 0.15\u20130.4.\r\n\r\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Asset Library, Sounds/Soundscape (Bed, Mid, Details)</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
