  m_text: 'Each audio file has import settings. Load Type decides how the clip sits in memory. Decompress On Load unpacks the whole clip when it loads: quick to play, large in memory, good for short details. Streaming reads it from disk while it plays: little memory, a little more CPU, good for long beds.



    <b>Predict:</b> The bed''s clip uses Load Type Streaming. If you change it to Decompress On Load, does what you hear change?



    <b>Try:</b>

    1. In the Project window, select Bed-Room-Tone in this scene''s Sounds folder.

    2. Set Load Type to Decompress On Load, click Apply, and read Imported Size at the bottom of the Inspector.

    3. Set it back to Streaming and click Apply.



    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Unity Manual: Audio Clip</color></size>'
